# expect: must point to a higher notation level
# modules: bpmn ddd
# Spec §7.2: refines goes strictly up (code -> design -> hub). BPMN and DDD are both design level, so a refines
# between them (either way) is not "up" — distinct notations, so the within-one-notation rule does not catch it.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix arch: <https://meta.linked.archi/core#> .
@prefix bpmn: <https://meta.linked.archi/bpmn/onto#> .
@prefix ddd:  <https://aisep.example/ont/ddd#> .
@prefix aisep: <https://aisep.example/ont/aisep#> .
@prefix : <https://aisep.example/model/t/> .

:t a arch:Model ; skos:prefLabel "测试模型"@zh .

:review a bpmn:UserTask ; arch:inModel :t ; skos:prefLabel "审核报价"@zh .
:quoting a ddd:DomainService ; arch:inModel :t ; skos:prefLabel "报价审核服务"@zh .
:rel-review-refines-quoting a arch:Refines ; arch:inModel :t ; arch:source :review ; arch:target :quoting .
